      "explanation": "The given logarithms have base \\(10\\), so changing to that base lets us use \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) directly:\n\\[\n\\log_5 12=\\frac{\\log_{10}12}{\\log_{10}5}.\n\\]\nSince \\(12=2^2\\cdot3\\), the product and power rules give\n\\[\n\\log_{10}12=2a+b.\n\\]\nAlso, \\(5=10/2\\), so\n\\[\n\\log_{10}5=1-a.\n\\]\nThis denominator is positive because \\(5>1\\). Therefore\n\\[\n\\log_5 12=\\frac{2a+b}{1-a},\n\\]\nwhich is choice D.",
      "id": "change-to-common-logarithms",
